  "status": "present",
  "value": "securities is a list of [symbol, P, S, A] rows with integer P >= 1, S >= 0 and A >= 0; funds is a non-negative integer. Buy a (possibly fractional) number of shares q_i with 0 <= q_i <= A_i and total cost sum(q_i * P_i) <= funds, maximising sum(q_i * S_i), the predicted value of the bought shares (unspent funds do not count). Return that maximum rounded half up to two decimals, as a string with exactly two digits after the point.",
